nc
Usage: nc [IPADDR PORT]

Open a TCP connection to IPADDR:PORT and wire it to stdin and stdout.
Every text tool you already know therefore works across a network.

	nc example.org 80
	printf 'GET / HTTP/1.0\r\n\r\n' | nc example.org 80

NOT compiled in on vos: listen mode. Upstream busybox can take -l and
-p to accept an incoming connection, but CONFIG_NC_SERVER is off in this
build, so nc here can only make outbound connections. A stick you carry
onto machines you do not own has no business opening a listening socket
by default.

nc is plaintext. For anything that matters, use tlstunnel.

See also: tlstunnel, wget, ping
